mike (Nebula): Hey team — onboarding hit a wall this morning. Our web app spikes parallel SDK init calls on first user action and ~5% of preflight requests return 429s. Seeing a bunch of failed UX flows.

lina (CSE): Sorry you're hitting that, mike. Can you paste a small sample of the error payloads / headers? Is it preflight or the generation call itself?

mike (Nebula): It's preflight (auth handshake). Sample response: `HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests` with body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\",\"retry_after\":1}`. Headers include `x-request-id` and `x-rw-rate-window: 60s`. We ramped from 0 -> 120 concurrent users in ~30s.

carlos (eng): Thanks — that pattern matches a thundering-preflight case. Are you using ephemeral token per client or shared token? Also what's your SDK version?

mike (Nebula): Using browser SDK v0.8.3 and ephemeral token for each session (we create on signin).

lina (CSE): Ephemeral-per-session + parallel preflight is the usual source. Two short mitigations to try:
- debounce the SDK init so multiple tabs / concurrent UI events coalesce
- reuse a short-lived token cache for N seconds to avoid simultaneous fresh preflight

carlos (eng): Also add jittered exponential backoff on 429s in the preflight path. Example pseudocode we recommend:```
const maxRetries = 4;
for (let i=0;i<maxRetries;i++){
  try { await preflight(); break }
  catch (e){ await sleep((Math.pow(2,i)*100) + jitter()) }
}
```

mike (Nebula): Ok that makes sense. Any short-term workaround on our side if we need to cut the ramp for the immediate demo today?

anna (CSM): We can request a temporary rate window increase on the account while engineering implements debounce/backoff. Lina — can you confirm account health and whether we have quota headroom?

lina (CSE): I'm checking now. Account shows normal usage; no long-term quota caps, but preflight fanout is hitting the per-minute session allocation. I can open a one-off escalation to operations for a short burst uplift.

carlos (eng): If you can provide the app domain and an expected ramp timeline we can coordinate a soft bump. Also share logs with x-request-ids and timestamps so we can correlate at the edge.

mike (Nebula): Domain: nebula.app. Ramp plan: demo tomorrow 10:00 PT, expecting 250 concurrent session in first 60s. I'll attach recent log snippet.

lina (CSE): Filing ops request now. @deploy-bot please create escalation ticket for account "Nebula" — temporary preflight burst increase for demo window 2026-03-22 17:00 UTC (10:00 PT).
deploy-bot: Escalation created: INC-2026-NEBULA-117 — ops notified, requested 2x short-term burst. ETA for response: ~2 hours. :white_check_mark:

carlos (eng): In parallel: a couple of quick SDK patches we can try now — (1) client-side preflight coalescing (hold 200ms before creating token), (2) reuse token store with TTL 30s, (3) add 429 retry with jitter. I can paste a tiny patch snippet if you want.

mike (Nebula): Please paste, that'd be great.

carlos (eng): Paste:```
// coalesce token creation: if another creation is pending, await it
let pending = null;
async function getEphemeral(){
  if (pending) return await pending;
  pending = createEphemeral();
  try { return await pending } finally { pending = null }
}
// reuse cache
const tokenCache = { value: null, expiresAt:0 };
async function token(){
  if (Date.now() < tokenCache.expiresAt) return tokenCache.value;
  const t = await getEphemeral();
  tokenCache.value = t; tokenCache.expiresAt = Date.now()+30000; // 30s
  return t;
}
```

mike (Nebula): Nice — we can wire that in quick. Any chance this release risk triggers renewal concerns? The customer success angle: we need to show we can stabilize for demo or they may delay contract.

anna (CSM): Noted — this is a short-term renewal risk. Lina, please include renewal owner in ops ticket and mark high-priority. I'll join the demo call and act as primary contact.

lina (CSE): Done — escalated with priority tag and renewal note. Ops acknowledged and asked for a final ramp test log after we apply client change.

carlos (eng): One more note — on the platform side we can add adaptive preflight caching for browser SDKs in the future to avoid per-session preflight storms. I'll log an internal feature ticket.

mike (Nebula): Thanks everyone. We'll push the coalescing + cache in a hotfix to staging now and run a 250-concurrent synthetic test. Will post results in this thread.

lina (CSE): Perfect. Quick checklist for follow-up: [ ] patch deployed to staging, [ ] synthetic ramp run (attach logs), [ ] ops approval confirmed, [ ] final demo smoke. Tag me when ready and I'll coordinate.

mike (Nebula): Patch in staging and synthetic ramp started — so far 0.5% 429s (down from 5%). Attaching first log snippet.

carlos (eng): Looks like the coalescing helped. We'll watch for edge cases (multiple tabs on different subdomains) but this is promising.

anna (CSM): I'll sit in the demo. Lina — if ops doesn't confirm the temporary bump in 1 hour ping me and I'll escalate to AM.

lina (CSE): Will do. Thanks all :raised_hands:
